"b31a7381-31bf-d212-1a72-0885d01c33c5","8c0b12f7-ee15-e79d-20e6-e1988983837d","dee73311-96e1-d829-785f-5ba8197048f5","c5fe5cc3-e7ff-16ea-a9ed-adf7e3648e7a","db823638-bca9-f4fa-3594-f3a502638d57","d16bb9ff-32c5-cd94-c4a0-d658ca548577","410efa0d-8bc6-9eb2-e236-158f8b034840","253a77bf-d706-5259-f0a0-f173557d8211","d6c34923-dfb2-0122-4760-7011582a8504","9319a614-243a-1101-7180-fbe0273dc242","3cad588b-8a0e-3e41-1035-ea7fb42f1b3d","2e717542-54a0-85e5-eadc-de714feb630c","2ce8348f-56ce-2582-0ba1-e1fd40afc15e","66ff2480-1846-c97c-1975-45a386818451","7ae9fd2c-4927-296b-70b7-8174f0e1f6c0","a9504977-1176-72f3-ee06-151ed5a6f6a3","64608836-7e89-db22-76b8-f8d97577e0a6","fda2580b-cd25-d64b-2fac-2f6349262b12","f0718f1d-c0f1-8b80-20ff-63eeb9104b15","a8296e88-b85b-dbe2-26f5-96c4c32f6474","78f2e7da-183a-38ed-e03e-16f0e619021a","c8de867a-1606-b40e-08cb-f6e561f95f6a","23f9d2c4-c52d-122e-b810-01ea9d658fcb","27ce87df-94e6-2391-ec9c-0f65f4f01278"],"reset":false,"shade":true,"mirror_uv":false,"autouv":0,"isOpen":false,"primary_selected":false}],"reset":false,"shade":true,"mirror_uv":false,"autouv":0,"isOpen":false,"primary_selected":false}],"textures":[{"name":"wall_hardwood.png","path":"","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","group":"","scope":0,"width":128,"height":128,"uv_width":128,"uv_height":128,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","file_format":"png","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","wrap_mode":"limited","pbr_channel":"color","fps":7,"frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"ad7fe0e5-1c1c-5448-af6e-64eb9dd2df8c","source":"data:image/png;base64,","relative_path":""}],"description":"# wall_hardwood\n\nHardwood wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Timber (dark squared hardwood timbers with iron bands), 3 m (106 u) with pointed tops and a fighting step behind at 78 u.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..109, z -7..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: finished 14, construction_0 19, construction_33 23, construction_66 27, ruined 28 (the state sets are cut from the finished cubes and map into the texture regions of the faces they were cut from).\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and footing with materials waiting, then walls rising inside scaffold).\n- `ruined`: broken walls at uneven heights, rubble and fallen beams.\n- `wall_hardwood_damaged.png`: damaged texture (cracks, scorch) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at x 0, z 2\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 78, 6)"}